 "asked_at": "2026-10-17T12:45+08:00",
 "answer": "Yes, the haze in KL is bad today. Air quality is in the **\"unhealthy\"** range.\n\n**Kuala Lumpur readings at 9.30am today, 17 October** (Air Pollutant Index, Department of Environment, via Malay Mail):\n- **Cheras:** 162\n- **Batu Muda:** 159\n- **Putrajaya:** 162\n\n**What the numbers mean:**\n- 0–50: Good\n- 51–100: Moderate\n- **101–200: Unhealthy** ← KL is here\n- 201–300: Very unhealthy\n- 300 and above: Hazardous\n\n**Nearby areas:** 24 areas across Malaysia had unhealthy readings this morning. Pasir Gudang in Johor was the highest at 196. Yesterday evening, Larkin and Pasir Gudang briefly reached 202, which is \"very unhealthy.\" The Klang Valley was also high yesterday, including Petaling Jaya at 173, Shah Alam at 168 and Klang at 176. The haze is coming from fires in Indonesia.\n\n**What you can do:**\n- Spend less time outdoors and skip outdoor exercise.\n- If you need to go out, wear a properly fitted N95 mask. Surgical masks don't filter haze well.\n- Keep windows closed and use an air purifier if you have one.\n- Take extra care with children, older people, pregnant women, and anyone with asthma, heart or lung conditions.\n\nReadings change through the day. For the latest numbers, check the DOE's APIMS website (eqms.doe.gov.my) or the MyIPU app.",
